  "goodToKnow": "Der Rumpf is the torso or trunk of the body (die Rumpfmuskulatur, core muscles), the hull of a ship and the fuselage of a plane. Das Rumpfparlament (rump parliament) is what remains after many members have left, like the Frankfurt Parliament's rump in Stuttgart in 1849. The verb rümpfen appears in die Nase rümpfen (to turn up one's nose). Plural: die Rümpfe."
